+# Tool Input Validation
+
+| Field  | Value                |
+| ------ | -------------------- |
+| Issue  | re-cinq/HALEngine#37 |
+| Status | In Progress          |
+
+`ToolRegistry.execute` in `src/orchestration/tools/registry.ts` validates `input` against the resolved tool definition's `inputSchema` before calling the tool executor. Validation enforces `required`, declared JSON Schema types and `enum` without injecting `additionalProperties: false`, coercing types or applying defaults, and returns any schema violation as a `ToolResponse` rather than throwing so `src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.ts` feeds the rejection back to the model within `maxToolRounds`.
+
+## Validation and error boundary
+
+- `ToolRegistry.execute` validates `input` against the resolved `inputSchema` before invoking the executor; when validation fails it skips the executor and resolves to a `ToolResponse` describing the failure so the orchestrator forwards that rejection as a `tool_result` for a corrected retry, while valid input (including unlisted extra properties) reaches the executor unchanged ([validated by: returns a schema rejection to the model so a corrected retry succeeds without calling the executor on bad input](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L16)).
+- Rejection results and log entries name the failing property paths and failed schema constraints (such as expected type) and never include any input property value, keeping both the offending value and sibling identifying fields out of returned text and logs ([validated by: names the failing field and expected type while omitting input values from both the rejection and the logs](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L58)).
+- Calling `execute` with an unregistered tool name still rejects with `Error('Unknown tool: <name>')`, so only a registered tool whose input violates `inputSchema` returns a rejection `ToolResponse`.
+
+## Schema compilation and dynamic definitions
+
+- Registering a static `ToolDefinition` compiles its `inputSchema` during `register` and throws synchronously naming the tool when the schema cannot be compiled ([validated by: throws at registration time naming the tool when a static inputSchema cannot be compiled](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L112)).
+- A static tool's `inputSchema` is compiled once at registration and reused across subsequent `execute` calls rather than recompiled per call.
+- Registering a function-valued `ToolDefinitionSource` resolves the definition on each `execute` call and validates against the `inputSchema` returned for that call, caching compiled validators by resolved schema object so a changed schema takes effect immediately ([validated by: validates each call against the schema a function-valued definition returns at that call](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L127)).
